      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/fair_oaks_arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Emerging in the mid‑19th century, Fair Oaks grew as part of the Arkansas Delta’s broader settlement patterns.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/fair_oaks_arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Located at 35°14′36″N 91°01′52″W, Fair Oaks sits on flat alluvial soil that fuels its farming.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/fair_oaks_arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "After WWII, Fair Oaks transitioned from cotton to soybeans and rice, driven by mechanization and federal support.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/fair_oaks_arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "By the 1880s, the St. Francis River rail line reached Fair Oaks, linking it to regional markets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/fair_oaks_arkansas"
    },
    {
